2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] Based on the `rohaTools` array in `slopfountain.ts`, there are 4 tools currently available:
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 1. read_time
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] Returns current local time with timezone and locale info.
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Parameters: None
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Returns: `{time, tz, locale}`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 2. submit_file
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] Accepts content from the model and saves it to the forge directory.
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Parameters:
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5]   - `contentType` (string) - MIME type
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5]   - `content` (string) - File content
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Returns: `{success, path}`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Action: Saves to `forge/submission-[timestamp].[ext]`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 3. fetch_file
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] Retrieves a file from the forge directory as base64.
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Parameters:
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5]   - `fileName` (string) - Path relative to forge/
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Returns: `{success, path, Base64}`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Action: Reads `forge/[fileName]` and returns base64-encoded data
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 4. tag_slop
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] Annotates shared content with metadata.
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Parameters:
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5]   - `name` (string) - Identifier
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5]   - `type` (enum: "code", "session", "share", "lode") - Category
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5]   - `description` (string) - Annotation text
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Returns: `{success, updated}`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] - Action: Updates `roha.tags` or share descriptions in the forge state
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] These are defined as OpenAI-compatible function schemas and passed to models when
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] `roha.config.tools` is enabled. The `onCall()` function handles the actual execution when models
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] invoke them.
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] The `processToolCalls()` function manages the round-trip: model generates tool_calls → `onCall()`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] executes → results pushed back to history as `role: "tool"` messages → recursive `relay(depth+1)`
2026-02-04 19:05:07 [kimi-k2.5] sends results to model.
