2026-02-08 23:04:13 [nitro@ryzen5] the files shared from the sloppy dir, is there any overlap with the main roha sources?
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] Minimal overlap. Architecturally distinct layers:
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] • Roha (`fountain/roha/`) = Core Server*
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `slopfountain.ts` - Main relay, model management, history
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `slopprompt.ts` - TCP server on 8081, raw stdin handler, NDJSON protocol definition
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] • Sloppy (`fountain/sloppy/`) = Client Connectors*
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `sloppybot.ts` - Discord client → connects to 8081
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `sloppylisten.ts` - SSH server → connects to 8081
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `sloppypipe.ts` - Unix socket → connects to 8081
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `sloppyhost.ts` - HTTP/JSON-RPC → uses `slophole.ts` worker to connect to 8081
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - `sloppyutils.ts` - Shared client connection logic (`connectFountain()`)
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] • Relationship:*
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - Protocol: Both sides use NDJSON (`{"messages":[{"message","from"}]}\n`)
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - Direction: Sloppy clients `Deno.connect()` to localhost:8081 where `slopprompt.ts` is
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] listening
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - No shared imports: Sloppy doesn't import from `../roha/`; it's a clean client/server
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] separation
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] • Redundancy check:*
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] - Connection logic appears in both but serves different roles:
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5]   - `slopprompt.ts:listenPort()` = accept connections (server)
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5]   - `sloppyutils.ts:connectFountain()` = initiate connections (client)
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] The sloppy directory is essentially a suite of protocol adapters (Discord, SSH, HTTP, Unix sockets)
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] that normalize external I/O into the fountain's NDJSON TCP protocol.
2026-02-08 23:04:45 [kimi-k2.5] 
