2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] Looking at the code, the cyclone emoji (🌀) used for OpenAI in `accounts.json` should render
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] correctly with proper width handling:
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] • Current Unicode Width Logic:*
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] In `slopprompt.ts`, the `stringWidth()` function handles U+1F300 (🌀) through the `isDoubleWidth`
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] range check:
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] [0x1F300, 0x1F6FF],  // Pictographs
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] This assigns it width 2 for terminal display.
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] For Discord rendering, `discordStringWidth()` assigns width 2.5 to the same range:
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] if (cp >= 0x1F300 && cp <= 0x1F5FF) return true;  // Returns 2.5
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] • Potential Issues to Check:*
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 1. macOS Terminal: The cyclone renders as width 2, but some macOS terminals (especially
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] with certain fonts) may treat emoji presentation selectors differently. The code skips variation
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] selectors (`0xFE0F`) which is correct.
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 2. Discord: The 2.5 width calculation is used for table alignment in Discord markdown. If
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] Discord's font renders 🌀 as a different width (some clients treat it as 2), table borders may
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] misalign.
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 3. VS Code: The code has special handling for VS Code (`vscodeNonce` check) that treats the
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] pail emoji (🪣) as thin (width 1), but this doesn't affect the cyclone.
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] • Recommendation:*
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] Add an explicit test in `slopspec.json` for the cyclone under "symbols" or add a specific width
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] override if Discord renders it differently than expected:
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] "🌀": {"char": "🌀", "codepoint": "1F300", "name": "CYCLONE", "wide": 2}
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] Or check the actual Discord rendering - if it's appearing as width 2 instead of 2.5 in Discord's
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] monospace blocks, you may need to adjust the `discordStringWidth` logic or add a specific exception
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] similar to how 🏛️ (U+1F3DB) is handled as thin in some contexts.
2026-02-09 00:13:48 [kimi-k2.5] 
