2026-02-18 17:47:55 [scudmarks@discord] what is Open in Mod View in discord pull down menu for bot users
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] "Open in Mod View" in Discord's user context menu opens the Moderation View interface,
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] which provides a consolidated dashboard for reviewing:
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - User info — account age, join date, roles, IDs
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Moderation history — warnings, timeouts, kicks, bans, notes left by mods
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Recent messages — activity across channels (with quick jump links)
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Spam/raid detection flags — if Automod or safety systems triggered
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] For bot users specifically, it's mostly useful for:
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Checking the bot's permissions and role hierarchy at a glance
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Reviewing if the bot has been flagged by safety systems
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Leaving internal moderation notes about problematic bots
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] - Quick access to the bot's user ID and created timestamp
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 17:48:01 [kimi-k2.5] It's primarily a moderator tooling feature — regular members don't see this option. If
