2026-02-18 18:14:18 [scudmarks@discord] As a Slop Fountain integration, I have currently got the slopfountain replies routed directly to a bot (a parrot named sloppy) on discord.
2026-02-18 18:14:18 [scudmarks@discord] I would like to discuss other options, so when multiple models are in play, and multiple users are connected via different integrations, the fountain becomes an active social hub.
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Looking at your current setup, you have a linear pipeline: User → Fountain → Sloppy →
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Discord. To make this a true social hub with multiple models and users, you need to move from a
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] relay architecture to a message bus with routing logic.
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Here are architectural options leveraging your existing `slopBroadcast`, `rohaHistory`, and the
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] `forge` session system:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 1. Multi-Model Orchestration Modes
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Instead of `relay(0)` calling one model, implement conversation topologies:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Round-Robin Panel* (`/panel mode`)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - User message broadcasts to N models sequentially
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Each model sees the previous model's response in history
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Sloppy posts threaded replies: "Claude says…", "GPT says…"
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Users vote with reactions to select the "winner" that continues
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Debate Mode* (`/debate`)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Two models argue opposing sides
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - `rohaHistory` branches using your existing `sessionStack`/`pushHistory`
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Each model gets isolated context of just their side + the debate topic
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Sloppy relays both streams with "Pro:" and "Con:" headers
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Ensemble Mode* (`/ensemble`)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Parallel async relays (your `beginRelay()` is already async-capable)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Wait for all models, then use a "synthesizer" prompt to merge responses
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Post the synthesis as the official reply, with model attributions in a spoiler tag
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 2. Multi-Integration Routing Layer
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Your `listenService` on 8081 currently accepts single connections. Expand this to a room-based
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] pub/sub:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] // rooms: Map<roomId, Set<Connection>>
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] // Instead of slopBroadcast(content, emoji) → broadcast to all,
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] // route by context:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] type Route = {
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]   room: string;        // e.g., "discord-general", "irc-#ai", "web-ui-7"
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]   models: string[];    // which muts are active here
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]   users: string[];     // nics allowed to trigger relays
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]   visibility: 'public' | 'whisper' | 'fork'
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] }
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Integration Options:*
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - IRC Bridge: Connect to Libera.Chat #slopfountain — models participate as `kimi-k2`,
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] `claude-opus`, etc.
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Matrix Bot: Rich threading support, better for multi-model chains than Discord's flat
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] structure
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Web UI: Browser clients connect via WebSocket to 8081, get live typing indicators from
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] `relay()` progress callbacks
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Slack: Better file sharing integration for your `commitShares` workflow
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 3. Social Mechanics Using Existing Tools
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Your `tag_slop` and `annotateTag` system is already set up for collaborative curation:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Forking Conversations*
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - When a user says `/fork`, call `pushHistory()` — creates isolated branch
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Other users see "User started a tangent" and can `/join 3` (session index)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Sloppy posts to Discord threads to keep main channel clean
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Attribution & Presence*
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Modify `plainHistory()` to inject `[from@{integration}]` prefixes (you partially do this)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Add a `presence` map: who's typing in which room
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Use Discord's "typing" indicator API when `relay()` is waiting
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Reaction-Driven Routing*
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Sloppy adds vote reactions (🟢🔴🟡) to model outputs
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - After 30s, highest vote triggers the next relay automatically
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] - Store votes in `roha.counters` (you already have the counter system)
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 4. The "Social Forge" Pattern
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Your `forge.json` already tracks `mut` specs and `lode` credits. Extend this to social
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] graph:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] // In forge.json
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] {
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]   "lounge": {
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]     "activeModels": ["claude-opus@anthropic", "kimi-k2.5@moonshot"],
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]     "participants": {
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]       "skid@discord": {reputation: 42, preferredModel: "claude-opus"},
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]       "blob@irc": {reputation: 7, preferredModel: "kimi-k2.5"}
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]     },
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]     "topics": ["coding", "philosophy"]  // auto-tagged via tag_slop
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5]   }
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] }
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] • Credit Sharing: Your `bumpModel` already deducts from `lode.credit`. Add a pool
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] system* where users donate credits to a room budget — when the pool hits $0.50, the model stops
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] responding until refilled. Creates collaborative fundraising for long conversations.
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 5. Implementation Path
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Given your existing code, the lowest-friction upgrade:
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 1. Enable multi-connection on 8081 — your `listenService` likely accepts one conn; make it
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] a `for await (const conn of listener)` loop
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 2. Add room headers to NDJSON — modify `slopFountain()` in sloppybot to include `{"room":
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] "discord-main", ...}`
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 3. Thread mapping — map Discord thread IDs to `rohaHistory` branches using your
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] `sessionStack`
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 4. Model presence — when `relay()` starts, broadcast `{"typing": "kimi-k2.5"}`; when
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] `flush()` completes, broadcast the result
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] The key insight from your code: you already have `syncRelay` vs async modes. For a social hub, you
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] want async by default (so users can chat while models think), but with causal
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] ordering (use your `slopmark()` hex timestamps to reconstruct conversation flow across
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] distributed integrations).
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] Would you like to drill into the Discord threading model specifically, or explore the IRC/Matrix
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] multi-protocol bridge architecture?
2026-02-18 18:14:47 [kimi-k2.5] 
