2026-02-21 09:47:41 [nitro@ryzen5] common log levels in linux v windows
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] I can see you're listening for slop on port 8081. Regarding your question about common log levels
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] in Linux vs Windows:
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] • Linux/Unix Systems (syslog):*
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - EMERG (0): System is unusable
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - ALERT (1): Action must be taken immediately
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - CRIT (2): Critical conditions
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - ERR (3): Error conditions
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - WARNING (4): Warning conditions
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - NOTICE (5): Normal but significant conditions
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - INFO (6): Informational messages
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - DEBUG (7): Debug-level messages
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] • Windows Event Log:*
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - Critical (1): Highest severity
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - Error (2): Error conditions
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - Warning (3): Warning conditions
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - Information (4): Informational messages
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] - Verbose (5): Detailed debugging information
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] • Key Differences:*
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 1. Naming conventions: Linux uses syslog levels (0-7), Windows uses descriptive names
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 2. Default facilities: Linux has separate facilities (kern, user, mail, etc.), Windows
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] categorizes by source
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 3. Storage: Linux typically uses text files (/var/log), Windows uses binary event logs
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 4. Tools: Linux uses `journalctl`, `tail`, `grep`; Windows uses Event Viewer, PowerShell
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] cmdlets
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] Both systems support similar severity concepts but implement them differently in their logging
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] architectures.
2026-02-21 09:48:03 [deepseek-chat] 
