2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] Based on the distance of 100 meters, I'd recommend walking rather than driving. Here's why:
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] • Walking is better for this distance:*
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - 100 meters is a very short distance - about a 1-2 minute walk
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - By the time you get in your car, start it, drive 100m, park, and get out, you'd likely spend more
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] time than just walking
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - You save fuel and reduce emissions for such a short trip
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - You get some light exercise
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - No need to find parking at the car wash
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] • When driving might make sense:*
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - If you have mobility issues or are carrying heavy cleaning supplies
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - If the weather is extremely bad
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] - If you need to transport cleaning equipment that's difficult to carry
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-02-21 11:03:38 [deepseek-chat] But for most people, walking 100m to the car wash is the most practical and efficient choice.
